# Confirmed live tonight: a more-specific literal-path rule placed AFTER a wildcard
# rule for the same header does NOT reliably override it on Cloudflare Pages - a
# deployment with /assets/world-map.js etc. explicitly set to `no-cache`, placed right
# after this exact /assets/*.js block, still served the wildcard's `immutable` value
# from origin (verified via a live response header + confirming that deployment really
# was the active one, ruling out a stale/failed deploy). Rather than depend on
# undocumented precedence behavior, the wildcard itself now only matches the one
# pattern that's actually safe to cache forever - esbuild's content-hashed
# tank-shared-<HASH>.js chunks, where a new build means a new URL, so a stale cache is
# never reachable. Every other .js/.css under /assets/ (world-map.js, tank-page.js,
# tank-article-deck.js, analytics-beacon.js, static-site.js, heat-score-v4.js,
# public-site.css, and all *.css) builds to the same filename every deploy, so it
# defaults to no-cache - still cacheable (a 304 skips the re-download when nothing
# changed), just never able to go stale for a year the way tonight's bugs did twice.
/assets/tank-shared-*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

/assets/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

# The interactive world-map raster sits at /assets/ (it travels through the esbuild
# bundle, not /assets/images/) under a FIXED name that gets swapped in place on art
# updates - without this rule it matches no pattern at all and falls through to the
# platform default, so users could hold stale art while the no-cache world-map.js
# (with its recalibrated hotspots) updates under them. Literal path, matched by no
# wildcard above, so the precedence caveat in the comment up top doesn't apply.
/assets/world-map-interactive.webp
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

# Unlike the JS chunks above, nothing under either of these two paths has a
# content-hashed filename - it's all fixed names (logo, Mud Puppy art, world map,
# the OG share image, banners) that CAN be updated in place, exactly like world-map.png
# /webp and og-share-world-map.jpg just were tonight. No hashed subset to carve out
# here, so no precedence question either - just no-cache outright.
/assets/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

# Per-article matchup cards (<slug>.jpg for social unfurls, <slug>-article.webp for
# the image the article itself shows). Fixed names regenerated in place on every
# build, so they're updatable exactly like the images above - and until now they
# matched no rule here at all and fell through to the platform default.
/assets/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

# Card-interior video (fixed filename, updatable in place, so not immutable) - but at
# 1.4MB a revalidation-per-open is real weight, so let it sit for a day and serve
# stale while revalidating rather than no-cache like the images above.
/assets/videos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

# / is served by functions/index.ts (session-dependent SSR; the function sets its own
# Cache-Control - _headers never applies to Function responses). This rule only governs
# the static dist/index.html fallback, which must also never sit in a shared cache
# since the real route serves per-session HTML at the same URL.
/
  Cache-Control: private, no-store

